WEBVTT

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:07.440
STUDIO RIKKA

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.160
In the future, probably Japan.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.160
Robots have long been put into practical use,

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:19.160
and practical use of androids has just begun.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.540
X has left the room.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.700
Will arrive shortly.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.000
It doesn't matter how real they look,

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:56.910
<i>No matter now real they look,</i>

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.790
<i>they're not flesh-and-blood humans.</i>

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.840
<i>So, regarding the existence of androids made for sexual intercourse -</i>

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.140
<i>Sexroids are just an urban myth!</i>

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.000
The low birthrate is just gonna get worse.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.830
<i>You're wrong! People are making such a fuss -</i>

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.900
Love. It isn't there.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.000
Ethics Committee

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.380
Isn't this commercial on a lot these days?

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.080
Status, Rikuo.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.850
He left at 12:03 P.M.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.700
He said he will have lunch out.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.250
It's really none of my business,

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.100
but don't you have anything better to do in the afternoons?

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.400
Playing hookey?

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:40.170
It's a substitute holiday.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.200
Not the kind of thing a waitress should be saying.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.690
Sorry! Rikuo aside,

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.900
I'd thought Masaki was a bit of a delinquent.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.000
He's an honors student.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.000
Probably comes as a surprise.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.230
You talk too much.

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.400
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.220
Hey, there are other people here you can talk with, too.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.310
Do you always carry that with you?

00:01:58.570 --> 00:01:59.900
There's lots I want to shoot.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.310
Well, I'll get around to it eventually.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.590
Thank you for the meal.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:03.700
You're welcome.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.790
I'll bring your after lunch Evlend.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:08.710
Evlend . . . Evlend . . .

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:09.860
What are you talking about?

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.500
It doesn't sound strange anymore!

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.490
You can't have my reading glasses -

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.370
Chie, give them back!

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:17.370
I'm a cat!

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:20.300
I suppose there's not much point in just sitting here.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.490
I just want to know what's up with this cafe.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:25.500
I'm not interested in getting all chummy with robots.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.570
Akiko's the only one we know about.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:28.620
What about that?

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.460
Over to the right.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.500
An android-holic with his android.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.670
No further explanation needed.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:41.970
What are you looking at?

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:42.850
Hey, you -

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:43.580
I wasn't looking!

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:43.900
You were!

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:44.400
I said, I wasn't!

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:44.910
No, you were!

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:45.410
I wasn't looking!

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:45.920
You were!

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:46.500
I wasn't looking!

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:47.160
You were!

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.030
You sure get along well.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:48.910
No way!

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:48.910
Never heard that before!

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.850
It's too bad, you two having such a good time all by yourselves.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:52.900
Next time you ogle -

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:53.910
I wasn't looking!

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:54.790
At what?

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.930
So, you're jealous of Koji.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.240
You've got it all wrong!

00:02:58.600 --> 00:02:59.670
Fascinating, isn't it?

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:02.110
Hey!

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.680
Why not come over here?

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.490
Time of Eve house rule:

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.360
No discrimination between humans and robots.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.310
It's dark! It's scary!

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.450
Wouldn't it be better not to meddle?

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.050
Is this meddling?

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.980
I think it would be wise to leave things up to the individual.

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:23.720
The conversation will be livelier with four, right?

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:26.830
Eve's Lovers

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:42.560
This is Koji.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.800
I am Rina.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.120
Ah, hello.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:49.660
I'm Masaki.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.590
He's Rikuo.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.210
You look again and I'll slap you.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.420
I wasn't looking!

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:54.260
Or was I?

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.080
Unconsciously, huh?

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.000
You get along well.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.530
Never heard that before!

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.530
No way!

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:58.850
Or have I?

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.130
You seem to come here a lot.

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:21.660
Yes.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.690
You come together?

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:30.930
No. Separately.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.270
Conversation seems to be going spendidly well.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:42.720
That's a Cinema Tide?

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:46.700
Can I take a look?

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:50.900
Does he like gadgets?

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:53.810
It's beautiful.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.180
Can you see a preview?

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:56.580
He's probably just making conversation.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.040
The capacity's huge!

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:00.890
'Cause I put in 500.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.240
It's M-LINK, so probably . . .

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.770
Cinetai is great, just as I'd thought!

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.170
So, that's about it . . .

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:35.480
How do you disconnect it?

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.750
What is this?

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.040
It's not what you think.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:57.460
It's so distant . . .

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.230
. . . your heart.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:01.540
No matter how often we meet,

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:02.690
or how often we are together . . .

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.790
I feel unsettled . . .

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.390
Finally, I understand why.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.990
Don't leave me on my own.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.250
What a drama.

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:20.100
Is it my fault?

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.170
I reckon so.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:22.710
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:24.550
What's the matter?

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:26.550
Did I do something?

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:28.500
I'll be right back.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.720
What happened?

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:31.900
What shall we say . . .

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.070
. . . a bloodbath?

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.690
X has arrived.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.560
I protected my master.

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:24.710
Then what about Koji -

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.370
What have I been doing until now - ?!

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:29.550
It seems the emergency repair was incomplete.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.250
So you come here for Koji . . .

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.500
. . . for your, I mean, your master's protection?

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.710
No, I come here on my own will.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:37.570
Shouldn't that be sent to the manufacturer for repairs?

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.600
I can't have anything to do with the official manufacturer.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.400
If the manufacturer found out about me,

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.890
it would cause trouble for my master.

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:53.400
More than that,

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.260
I want to stay here, even just a little bit longer.

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:57.170
. . . won't even go for repairs . . .

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:03.000
At this cafe, I'm the one who acts least human.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.260
Isn't that correct?

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:09.590
I wouldn't be strange if I were destroyed at any moment.

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:12.620
I have no use for my learning functions,

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:15.630
and it seems I'm resisting them on my own accord.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:18.890
Koji . . .

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:22.120
He treats me, in this state, as a human woman.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:25.240
So I think that here . . .

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.010
I am happy.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.320
. . . but,

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:31.040
that woman in the photo . . .

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:31.940
You are kind, aren't you.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:34.470
But it's okay,

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:36.280
because Koji's kindness won't change.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.480
. . . after all . . .

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:44.310
. . . I'm going back.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.550
But!

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.350
The coffee -

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.470
. . . the flavor of the coffee changed,

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.970
. . . at first I was angry, but -

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:02.790
. . . after I understood, I got just a little bit happy.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:05.680
. . . even though it isn't a human being.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:08.440
Tell Koji!

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:09.850
Tell him what you want to say!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.380
. .. even if it's to a human being!

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.570
Why do you think that?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.230
You understand, don't you?

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.770
You know how that feels.

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:26.720
Yes, I think so.

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:31.220
I can't believe the things I'm saying.

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:33.620
So this one is for real?

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:36.530
Something has been bugging me.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:40.480
There's not a single shot of you and Rina together.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.920
There's no way you could take a photo like that.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:46.260
It's be bad if people found out about your make-believe lover.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.550
Or is this one a robot too?

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:49.870
She's not a robot!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:50.930
All the more.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:52.260
What are you doing at this cafe?

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:53.700
We're not make-believe lovers!

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.350
So you're saying it's for real?

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:59.880
That there's love?

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.910
Don't try telling me crap like that.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:09.660
Here's what you're trying to say.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:13.120
For humans, a human partner is best.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.200
So you do get it.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:18.640
I get it.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:20.800
I understand.

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.150
Just like you say, Rina and I

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:26.260
are nothing but a relationship between a human and android.

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:28.680
There are things we can't understand about each other -

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:30.320
As if you could possibly understand each other -

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:33.450
I . . .

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:36.340
I just want to help my master.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:39.760
What?!

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:45.890
My master has a lot in common with Rina.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.160
I want to help my master.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:58.490
Yesterday, again, I saw lots of different people.

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:01.080
I'm not interested in those things.

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:08.960
But, Master . . .

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:13.120
Master should find a new partner.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:14.630
A human -

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.250
I've had enough . . .

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:21.200
I'm tired . . .

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:22.580
Koji is best for me.

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:24.080
I'll become a robot.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:27.800
Always stay with me.

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:30.310
Master is completely dependent on me.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:32.930
But I didn't know what to do.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:34.770
When I met Rina,

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:36.710
I thought this person is just like my master.

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.270
Her gestures toward me,

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:42.500
and the expressions she sometimes shows me.

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:45.350
I want to get to know Rina better, so I can understand my master.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:47.510
I want to help my master.

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:50.120
The First Law.

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:52.050
About all this . . .

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:54.210
Can you keep quiet about it to Rina?

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.000
The cafe's rule?

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.940
I don't want to hurt anyone.

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:03.450
Selfish.

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:05.950
Pathetic person.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.660
But everyone can't be happy.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:25.790
Thanks.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:29.590
Let's clear out of here.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.940
So, excuse us.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:42.320
There sure are lots of different types.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.420
Humans?

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.210
Androids, too.

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:50.320
I was wrong to hit you.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:51.740
You were right.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:54.550
I should have taken a good look, too.

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:58.780
Masaki . . .

00:12:58.880 --> 00:12:59.830
Yeah?

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:01.430
You've seen the light?

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:02.780
Like I'm an adolescent junior high schol kid!

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:11.650
But Rina's the one who is -

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:12.970
No, it's the other way around!

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:22.180
Just a sec -

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:23.680
What did Rina say?

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.010
So you come here for Koji . . .

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:28.640
. . . for your, I mean, your master's protection?

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:29.880
No, I come here on my own will.

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:33.260
Master

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:33.140
Didn't say a single thing about Koji being master.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:34.360
Didn't say anything.

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:36.040
Outside the cafe . . .

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:37.640
Master                            Master

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.810
those two have nothing to do with each other?

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:38.470
But, they both say they're with a human.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:38.980
Master      Master

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:40.450
They're contradicting each other.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:41.380
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:45.400
Maybe they haven't noticed. Each other, I mean.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:47.340
That's all the hints you're getting.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.470
Human       Human

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:52.690
They're the same.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:53.680
Explain yourself.

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:56.340
We can't figure out if we're talking to a human or android.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:57.900
And androids are the same!

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:00.350
Those two are interested in each other -

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.470
For different reasons.

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:03.900
They both have things they're hiding from one another -

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.570
What do you mean?

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:07.850
Just like ordinary love.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.620
You're saying some nice things.

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:11.990
But don't meddle too much.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:15.180
Love between androids.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.180
Fake love.

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:18.290
So what about the woman in the photo the other day?

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:21.680
Androids in a love triangle.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:26.810
Androids getting tangled up in foolish passion?

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:28.420
Hey, cut out the peculiar comments!

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:30.530
I'll find out the truth someday.

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:31.700
Oh . . . really . . .?

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:41.280
Master, welcome home.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:45.480
Nao and mom gone to dinner!

00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:47.300
Sammy, take care of the rest!

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:50.570
What's that in your hair?

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:54.660
Does it not please you?

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:50.830
Second half of the first season resumes spring 2009!
